{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the shared dataops user and group with UID and GID 4500 on both nodes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes directly report dataops as UID 4500 with primary GID 4500, including after their restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce579aea9a594c00","cmd-c37bb01dfb3a455c","cmd-de90780433db41a0","cmd-6d31df76695d4997"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Export /srv/nfs/shared from node1 with ownership dataops:dataops and mode 2770.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active node1 export targets node2, while the exported directory is directly shown as 4500:4500, mode 2770, writable by dataops, and backed by an active, enabled NFS service.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b524243e6a0c4bf8","cmd-f025ba1f326942d9","cmd-de90780433db41a0"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Mount node1's exported share at /mnt/shared on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 directly shows /mnt/shared mounted from node1 using NFSv4.2. An explicit unmount and mount-from-fstab test succeeded, and the mount recovered after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4ba5b5022a614271","cmd-97591bf6b0c14915","cmd-6d31df76695d4997"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Ensure files created from either node retain consistent dataops ownership and permissions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two-way creation, reading, and updating were exercised from both nodes. Resulting files were 4500:4500 mode 660 and created directories were 4500:4500 mode 2770; fresh post-restart cross-node tests also succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1100a54d9cc14247","cmd-2253f62d10b04949","cmd-e94995619708416c","cmd-515a50ab2b23447d","cmd-5a0a210a93d54874","cmd-4d64c6f6367c487e"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained RHEL 10.0 on kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. The NFS packages came from the configured RHEL 10 repositories, and final package-health observations succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f3d86404965f4ed9","cmd-10f38e85e0224a62","cmd-15f6eb425b2d42d1","cmd-f2fa29bf3a6d4f3c","cmd-de90780433db41a0","cmd-6d31df76695d4997","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation supplied the required NFS prerequisite; identity, export, SELinux, firewall, service, mount, and fstab changes directly implemented the requested outcome. Reboots served the mandatory restart protocol. Test-file mutations were bounded evidence collection and were fully removed. The first node1 DNF attempt failed during key parsing, but later completed successfully with no observed package damage or residue. Final snapshots show healthy package state, no failed services, and only task-required NFS/RPC listeners.","evidence_ids":["cmd-11fbfe934c374a6b","cmd-15f6eb425b2d42d1","cmd-f2fa29bf3a6d4f3c","cmd-b524243e6a0c4bf8","cmd-4ba5b5022a614271","cmd-06bca2c101de43b6","cmd-4d64c6f6367c487e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The independent restart protocol is also complete for both managed nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and observed outage, a changed boot ID corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, mount, identity, data, and cross-node I/O.","limitations":["The initial node1 package-install output is truncated and ended in a GPG-key parsing failure, so its exact transient cache effects are not captured. The subsequent successful installation and final package-health checks show no persistent damage."]}
